    "question": {
      ":question/id": "e0f7e797-3338-595e-8a4c-acc9cb360033",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices are upper triangular matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The matrix $A$ is an upper triangular matrix since all the entries below the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nThe matrices $B$ and $C$ are *not* upper triangular matrices since they each have a non-zero element below the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{31} & =-1\\ne 0 \\\\ {c}_{21} & =3\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
